True... anyone who actually reads this newsgroup would be hard pressed
to make anyone believe they never read any of the posts on it.
I have ascended 4 times. The very first time was soon after I signed
onto this newsgroup after a long hiatus (when I stopped playing before
we were still on 3.0). I tried to play as if non of the information
I picked up via rec.games.hack was known to me, to see exactly what
was, or was not possible. And I can assure just about everyone that
the game is nigh on impossible without spoilers. I eventually
had to give in and use my ill-gotten bell/book/candle knowledge to
get down to the bottom level. But other then that, everything else I
did merely on my 3.0 and earlier knowledge. And the came was quite
playable other then that.

People keep saying oh... but the Oracle will tell you of the
bell/book/candle deal... All I can say to that is bullshit. =)
I went to the bottom of Gehonomm and back up, and didn't have enough
cash to get the Oracle to tell me anything... (well she did tell me
all sorts of things... but certainly nothing on the the entering that
last level) And without spoilers
I'd not even know of the existance of Fort Ludios (have never been
there, despite knowing it exists somewhere), so that is not a
source of income. A player simply does not have enough gold to get
any useful information from teh Oracle on the way down. And coming 
back much much later when you might possibly have enough only to
have her not tell you anything you can use is a pain in the least.

The game DEFINITELY needs a better source of clues on how to
deal with the vibrating square. The quest leader would be perfect
for that.
As to the need to give clues on some of the other things (ie:
the hidden magic portals, and medusa, et al) I saw no need...
but that was because my class of first ascension was a knight
with Excalibur so the searching atribute found them for me without
any prompting, and being a long time player of Hack 1.0 through to
Nethack 3.0 the snake haired ugly one was not a new experience.

I have to admit.. that playing the game without spoiler information
is infinitely more rewarding. Dave the Knight had a bitch of a time
on the elemental levels simply because I knew nothing at all about them.
(The air level killed me until I tried a Levitate spell on a whim.
 The water level is a really scare place when you have no idea what the
 hell is going on... nor any clue that such a thing as an amulet of
 magical breathing exists... much less own one of the same)

In my oppinion. Spoilers ruin much of the fun of the game. Which is
why it is a crying shame that the game is impossible without them.
Definite design flaw.

